---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactModal from '../components/ContactModal.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service | Jevans Consulting"
  description="Read the website and service terms for Jevans Consulting, including how project proposals, payments, intellectual property and client responsibilities are agreed."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Header />
    <main id="top" class="privacy-page">
      <article class="privacy-policy">
        <a class="projects-back" href="/#top">&larr; Back to home</a>
        <br/>
        <span class="projects-eyebrow">WORKING TOGETHER</span>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: 26 November 2026</p>

        <p>This page explains how to use the Jevans Consulting website and gives general information about our services. Jevans Consulting is run by Jason Evans, an independent consultant based near Cannock Chase, Staffordshire. It does not itself create a contract for paid services. Any project contract will be set out separately in a written proposal or agreement.</p>

        <h2>Website information</h2>
        <p>The website provides general information about website design, development and digital support services. We aim to keep information accurate and up to date, but it is not a binding offer and may change. A project begins only when both parties agree the scope and terms in writing.</p>

        <h2>Project proposals and agreements</h2>
        <p>Before work starts, we will provide a written proposal or agreement describing the agreed work, deliverables, timescales, fees, payment arrangements, revision limits, ongoing support (if any), and how changes or cancellation will be handled. That document forms the agreement for the project and takes priority over this general page if the two conflict.</p>
        <p>Website package prices and care plan details shown on this site are general descriptions. The written proposal or agreement will confirm what is included for your project. We will not begin chargeable work until the scope and price have been agreed.</p>

        <h2>Client responsibilities</h2>
        <p>You agree to provide the information, content, approvals and access reasonably needed for the agreed work, and to make sure you have the rights or permissions needed for materials you supply. If delays or requested changes affect the agreed scope or timing, we will discuss any impact with you and agree changes before proceeding.</p>

        <h2>Fees, payment and cancellation</h2>
        <p>For website packages, the site describes a 50% deposit to secure the project, with the remaining balance due before launch. Any exceptions or project-specific payment dates will be stated in the written proposal. Additional work outside the agreed scope will be discussed and approved, including its cost, before it begins.</p>
        <p>Care plans are described as monthly services with no long-term contract and 30 days' notice to leave. Your agreement will confirm the plan, monthly fee, included support and how to give notice. We will not add charges for work outside the agreed scope without discussing and agreeing them with you first.</p>
        <p>If you are a consumer, any applicable statutory rights—including cancellation rights for certain distance contracts—continue to apply. We will provide information about any relevant cancellation period and process before you enter into a contract. Nothing in these terms removes rights that cannot legally be excluded.</p>

        <h2>Ownership and permissions</h2>
        <p>Unless a written agreement says otherwise, the website's text, design, branding and other materials belong to Jevans Consulting or the relevant rights holder. You may view and print pages for your personal use, but you must not republish or commercially use website materials without permission.</p>
        <p>Ownership, licensing and handover of work created for a client—including source files, code, content and third-party assets—will be described in the project agreement. Third-party software, hosting, fonts, plugins or other services may have their own licence terms and fees.</p>

        <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>
        <p>Projects may rely on third-party platforms or services such as hosting providers, domain registrars, payment processors or software vendors. Those services are provided under their own terms and privacy policies. We are not responsible for changes, outages or decisions made by those providers, but we will explain relevant dependencies as part of the project where appropriate.</p>

        <h2>Liability and legal rights</h2>
        <p>Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability where the law does not allow it, or affects your legal rights as a consumer. Any responsibilities and remedies relating to paid work will be set out in the project agreement and applicable law. We do not guarantee specific search ranking, traffic, sales or business results unless a written agreement expressly says otherwise.</p>

        <h2>Questions or complaints</h2>
        <p>If you have a question or concern about these terms or a project, please get in touch using the <a href="/#contact">contact form</a>. We will work with you to understand the issue and agree a practical next step.</p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these website terms when the site or our services change. The date above shows when this page was last updated. Updates to an existing project agreement will be discussed with you and agreed in writing.</p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>These website terms are governed by the law of England and Wales. If you are a consumer living elsewhere in the UK, this does not remove any mandatory protections available to you under the law that applies where you live.</p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
  <ContactModal />
</Layout>
